Part 1: Problem 4 Consider the following models where ${e_t}$ is a $0$ mean white noise process with variance $σ^2$. \begin{enumerate} \item [i] $Y_t = 1.9 Y_{t−1} − 0.9 Y_{t−2} + e_t − 0.5e_{t−1}$ \item [ii] $Y_t = 0.5 Y_{t−1} + e_t − 0.2e_{t−1} − 0.15e_{t−2}$ \end{enumerate}
Part (a) \fbox{Write each model above using backshift notation.}
\begin{enumerate} \item [(i)] $(1 - 1.9 \backshift + 0.9 \backshift^2) Y_t = (1 - 0.5 \backshift) e_t$.
